This repository uses `lehard/dev-platform` with `workflow_profile={{ workflow_profile }}` and `publish_mode={{ publish_mode }}`.

Project/domain documentation belongs here; the central platform owns only reusable development process.

## First checks

```bash
python3 scripts/platform_doctor.py
python3 scripts/agent_doctor.py
```

`platform_doctor.py` checks the installed platform contract and OpenSpec compatibility. `agent_doctor.py` checks current GitHub/Git readiness for starting or finishing work.

## Working on a change

For non-trivial product or architecture work, create/update the OpenSpec change first. If implementation changes direction, update the relevant OpenSpec artifact before code knowingly diverges.

Start through the shared profile-aware entrypoint:

```bash
python3 scripts/start_task.py my-change --task "OpenSpec my-change: task range" --scope "path/or/module"
```

Run selected checks before completion:

```bash
python3 scripts/select_checks.py
python3 scripts/select_checks.py --execute
```

Publish through:

```bash
python3 scripts/finish_task.py
```

The finish step re-fetches `origin/{{ main_branch }}` and either creates a PR or performs a guarded direct push according to `.dev-platform.toml`. It never force-pushes or auto-resolves divergence.

For non-trivial OpenSpec changes, run `/opsx:verify` before archive in addition to project-specific tests/QA.

Reusable CI is pinned to `{{ platform_ci_ref }}`, not `dev-platform@main`.

See `AGENTS.md` and `docs/engineering/`.
